mean_and_second_item.plain, line 2: Write "average" instead of "mean", or use 's for a field called "mean".

    show the mean of the amounts of sales
         ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
Try one of these:
    show the average of the amounts of sales
  or
    show (the amounts of sales)'s mean
Why: "mean" has other everyday meanings, like "unkind", so Plain says "average".

mean_and_second_item.plain, line 4: Write "item 2 of" instead of "the second item of", or use 's for a field called "second item".

    show the second item of colors
         ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
Try one of these:
    show item 2 of colors
  or
    show colors's second item
Why: Plain picks an item by its number, counting from 1, so the second item is "item 2 of".

mean_and_second_item.plain, line 5: Write "it" instead of "each".

    show colors where each is "red"
                      ^^^^
Try this:
    show colors where it is "red"
Why: Inside "where", "it" means each item being checked, as in: the scores where it is more than 80

